\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Enhancements in Mega2 version 4.6.1
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 can now produce PLINK/SEQ format files and a script for loading these
 files into a PLINK/SEQ project (See section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Detailed-info-PSEQ"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug fix: Mega2 4.6.0 had broken support for Linkage format input when using
 a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Names file
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 (See section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Names-file"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Added binaries for native Microsoft Windows 8 and MinGW built on Microsoft
 Windows 8.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Enhancements in Mega2 version 4.6.0
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 is now much more memory-efficient.
 Mega2 now uses a compressed representation for storing two-allele markers,
 such as those typically encountered in a genome-wide association study
 (GWAS).
 For example, a GWAS study of 895,103 two-allele markers on 3,122 individuals
 requires only 1 Gigabyte of memory.
 For details, see section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Input-menu-item:"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 also provides a compressed representation for microsatellite markers,
 allowing up to 256 alleles.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Completely untyped family members do not require space for their allele
 values.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Enhancements in Mega2 version 4.5.9
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug fix: Mega2 will now compile properly on Red Hat (RHEL), CentOS, and
 Solaris systems.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
