\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 can now generate binary format PLINK files (See section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Analysis-PLINK-option"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 can now generate files for FBAT analysis (See section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Analysis-FBAT-option"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 can supports 5 non-human species, including dog, mouse, and horse
 (See section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Mega2-command-line-arguments"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
We have improved the handling of missing value codes for quantitative phenotypes
 and covariates, allowing the user to more easily map the missing value
 code in the input data files to the desired missing value code in the reformatt
ed output files.
 If the user uses a numerical output missing value code that is within the
 range of the real values, Mega2 warns the user.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 code files are now C++ files and require a C++ compiler.
 Internally, we have begun to use object-oriented paradigms to make it much
 easier to add new analysis options.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Enhancements in Mega2 version 4.5.5/4.5.6
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 can now read files in PLINK format.
 Both binary PED files (*.bed) and PED files (*.ped) are accepted.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 can now generate PLINK output MAP files that contain both genetic
 and physical maps.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 is now more robust in handling input map files containing multiple
 genetic and/or physical maps.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Mega2 is now more memory efficient and runs faster than previous versions.
 
\end_layout

