\begin_layout Subsubsection
PLINK binary PED input format
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Pedigree files
\series default
 for GWAS studies can become rather large and slow to process.
 The PLINK binary PED file makes these data more accessible.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This format is typically coded using three primary files: the pedigree file,
 the family file, and the map file.
 The default naming scheme is to use the same stem for all three, and a
 '.ped' extension for the pedigree file, a '.fam' extension for the family
 file, and a '.map' extension for the map file.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To instruct Mega2 to read binary PLINK format files, choose option 12 in
 the initial Mega2 input menu:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
12) Switch to PLINK input menu (binary format)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Binary PED file (*.bed)
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Binary-PED-file"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This file is described in detail in the PLINK manual.
 It tightly encodes the allele data in two bits per SNP.
 The file is not ASCII and not human readable.
\end_layout

