\begin_layout Subsection
LINKAGE input file formats
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sub:Linkage-file-formats"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The LINKAGE format is the one used by the LINKAGE programs (Lathrop and
 Lalouel 1984; Lathrop et al.
 1986; Lathrop and Lalouel 1988); these formats are described in detail
 in the LINKAGE User's Guide at 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\align center
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

http://linkage.rockefeller.edu/soft/linkage/
\end_layout

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
and also in the LINKAGE Handbook by Terwilliger and Ott (1994).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
LINKAGE format files typically come in pairs: the 'datain.dat' contains the
 locus information (disease model, allele frequencies, numbers of alleles,
 etc.), while the 'pedin.dat' contains the pedigree structure information
 and phenotypes.
 However, the original LINKAGE format made no provisions for locus names
 nor for marker map information.
 So Mega2 uses as input a trio of files which remedy these omissions:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the LINKAGE locus file modified to contain locus name information; 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the LINKAGE pedigree file; and 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the Mega2 map file.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
LINKAGE locus file
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sub:Locus-file"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\emph on
Default name:
\emph default
 datain.##, where ## is the number of the chromosome (01, 02,..., 23) or datain.ex,
 where ex is the input file extension.
 For example, if the chromosome number chosen is 2, then Mega2 looks for
 the file datain.02 in the current directory.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset VSpace defskip
\end_inset

The locus data file is in standard LINKAGE format with the addition of locus
 names, which must be specified.
 The standard (but not well-known) LINKAGE format for including loci names
 is to, right after the number of alleles, put a # sign followed by the
 marker name.
 For example:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code

\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
5 0 0 5  << NO.
 OF LOCI, RISK LOCUS, SEXLINKED (IF 1) PROGRAM
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
0 0.0 0.0 0  << MUT LOCUS, MUT RATE, HAPLOTYPE FREQUENCIES (IF 1)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1       2 3 4 5
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1   2   # TRAIT
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
 0.990000 0.010000   << GENE FREQUENCIES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1 << NO.
 OF LIABILITY CLASSES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
0.0000 1.0000 1.0000 << PENETRANCES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
0       2  # Q1
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
 0.990000 0.010000   << GENE FREQUENCIES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1 << NO.
 OF TRAITS
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1.000   10.000 20.000 << GENOTYPE MEANS
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1.000   << VARIANCE - COVARIANCE MATRIX
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1.000   << MULTIPLIER FOR VARIANCE IN HETEROZYGOTES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
3   2   # M1
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
 0.500000 0.500000   << GENE FREQUENCIES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
3   2   # M2
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
 0.500000 0.500000   << GENE FREQUENCIES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
3   2   # M3
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
 0.500000 0.500000   << GENE FREQUENCIES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
0 0  << SEX DIFFERENCE, INTERFERENCE (IF 1 OR 2)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
0.1     0.1 0.1 0.1  << RECOMBINATION VALUES
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1 0.10000 0.45000 << REC VARIED, INCREMENT, FINISHING VALUE 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This setup would give the name TRAIT to the first locus, the name Q1 to
 the second locus, and the name M1 to the third locus, etc.
 (You may put no space between the # sign and the locus name, if desired).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Each co-dominant marker name must have an exact match in the corresponding
 map file; if a locus name in the locus data file is not found in the map
 file, then the user is warned about this.
 If the user still chooses to proceed, any marker that was not found in
 the map file will not appear in any of the output files (as Mega2 would
 not know which map position to put it in).
 HINT: This feature can be used to easily exclude a marker from all files
 produced by Mega2 - simply alter the name of the marker in the map file
 so that it no longer matches.
\end_layout

