\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 tags.
 These three tags are case insensitive e.g.
 the ID tag can be any of 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

ID:
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Id:
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

iD:
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

id:
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 Unique IDs are allowed within the pre-makeped format pedigree file, but
 the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Ped:
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Per:
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 tags are not recognized.
 If these are provided, Mega2 simply ignores these fields as long as they
 are placed after the phenotype/genotype columns.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

There is no restriction on the ordering of Ped:, Per: and ID: field pairs
