name "VCFtools Options"
target "http://vcftools.sourceforge.net/options.html"

\end_inset

).
 In particular, the options supported are the: Site Filtering Options, the
 Individual Filters, and the Genotype Filters.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note that filtering must be done using position information and sample IDs
 from the input VCF file.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Input format: Variant Call Format files
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Pedigree and Map datafile
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The variant file in the selected format and the pedigree (.fam) are required
 for Variant input files.
 The phenotype file as well as the Mega2 map, omit, frequency and penetrance
 files are optional.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Input menu item: Variant Call Format datafile:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This specifies the vcf file name as .bcf, .vcf, or .vcf.gz as appropriate to
 the input type chosen.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Input menu item: Pedigree datafile:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This specifies the pedigree file name (.fam file).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Input menu item: Map datafile:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This specifies a Mega2 map file to provide genetic position information
 for analysis modes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Input menu items: Omit, frequency and penetrance data files (optional):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This specifies the names of the omit file, allele-frequency file and trait
 penetrance file respectively.
 The omit, frequency and penetrance input data files are all optional files.
 The frequency and penetrance files are read in only in the annotated file
 format.
 These files were created to support the Mega2 native file format, but we
 allow these files to be specified for PLINK and VCF file formats.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Input menu item: Output Directory: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This specifies the name of the directory where Mega2 creates the output
 files.
 By default, this is set to the directory from which Mega2 is invoked.
 The output directory can be specified either as an absolute path (e.g., /home/use
r/mega2_results/example) or a relative path.
 Mega2 checks to see if the specified directory exists, if not, the user
 is asked if this directory should be created before proceeding.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Input menu item: Simulating genotyping errors: 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sub:Simulate-errors"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option can be toggled between 
\emph on
yes
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
no
\emph default
 by simply selecting option 8 of the input menu.
 The default value is no.
 Setting this option to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

yes
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 will cause Mega2 to execute a genotyping error simulation step after selection
 and reordering of marker loci.
 In this step, genotypes of individuals are changed at user-selected marker
 loci, according to a user-specified error-probability model.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Genotyping error simulation 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Overview 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option was created in order to evaluate Genotyping error detection
 software.
 This allows the user to introduce errors at a certain percentage of genotypes
 within a marker, by changing the input genotype subject to certain requirements
 (such as allele frequencies, whether to select a homozygous or heterozygous
 genotype, etc.).
 This option can be turned on and off using in the Mega2 input menu.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Parameter selection menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The mistyping simulation step requires selection of loci at which errors
 should be introduced, the probability model for introducing errors, and
 names of the output files which contain lists of changed genotypes, and
 the percentage of genotypes changed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The error simulation menu is as follows: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Error model and loci selection menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
0) Done with this menu - please proceed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
1) Apply error model to selected loci.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
2) Apply error to all except selected loci.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
3) Select error model Uniform 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
4) Change error probability [0.050] 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
5) Mistyping genotypes file name error_genos.06 [new] 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
6) Mistyping summary file name error_sum.06 [new] 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Marker selection
\series default
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 Loci can be selected by two methods: (a) by specifying loci that should
 have errors, or, (b) specifying loci that should NOT have errors.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Error model selection
\series default
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 Currently input error probabilities can follow any one of three models:
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
One uniform error rate for all selected markers
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
A uniform rate means that alternate genotypes are selected with a uniform
 probability).
 The value of this probability is set to 0.05 by default, and can be changed
 via the menu.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Separate uniform error rates for each selected marker:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
These error rates have to be specified inside the map file as a 4th column
 under the heading 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

error
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 These rates cannot be changed once Mega2 has started running.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
SimWalk2's error model:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
This involves the specification of 5 separate error probabilities, which
 can be changed using the menu.
 For an explanation of these probability values, refer to the paper: 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\series bold
Detection and Integration of Genotyping Errors in Statistical Genetics
\series default
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 by Sobel et al.
 in AJHG, Vol 70: pages 496-508.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
