\begin_layout Standard
Mega2 has modest support for different species.
 Its model is that all chromosomes up to some number are autosomes.
 The last autosome is then followed by sex chromosome, 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

X
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Y
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, which have the next two numeric values.
 The pseudo XY chromosome number may be specified as well as the mitochondrial
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

chromosome
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

MT
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) number.
 For all chromosomes after the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

last autosome
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, letter designations should be used in Mega2 files for clarity.
 Note: Mega2 reserves the letter designation 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

U
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 for an unknown chromosome.
\end_layout

