\begin_layout Section
Running Mega2 in Batch mode
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Batch-mode"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Overview
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Mega2 can be run in a batch-mode by invoking it with a single argument which
 is a batch file name: 
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
begin{verbatim}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
> mega2 MEGA2.BATCH
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
end{verbatim}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This runs Mega2 in a non-interactive mode through the following steps: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Input Menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Analysis Menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Locus Reordering and Selection menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Trait Selection Menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Genotyping error simulation setup 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Output file names menu 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Input of default parameters
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the previous version, Mega2 started running in the interactive mode after
 the genotyping error simulation setup, and prompted the user to input analysis-
specific parameters, such as output file names etc.
 New batch file items have been implemented which makes user-interaction
 unnecessary for the bulk of the execution.
 Subsequent versions will be made fully automatic except for input data
 errors that cannot be ignored.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Each time you run Mega2 in interactive mode, a new batch file is created.
 This batch file is named MEGA2.BATCH, and the existing MEGA2.BATCH is moved
 into MEGA2.BATCH.old.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Using the 
\emph on
-
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
/
\end_layout

\end_inset

-
\emph default
nosave option 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The purpose of having a batch-execution mode is to enable Mega2 to be embedded
 within scripts, so as to be run automatically.
 A typical application of this feature would be running thousands of replicates
 of simulated data.
 In this case, mega2 should be run with the 
\emph on
-
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
/
\end_layout

\end_inset

-
\emph default
nosave (short option -x) option, so that summary files for each run are
 not saved in a separate directory as below: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
         mega2 --nosave batch_file
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
         mega2 -x batch_file
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The online check for the latest release is automatically disabled in the
 batch mode.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Batch file format 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The batch file is a text file which has a specific format.
 Each line is either a comment or a definition.
 Blank lines are ignored.
 Comment lines begin with a 
\series bold
#
\series default
 in the first column.
 A definition line has two parts, a name and a value.
 Each definition line is of the form: 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\emph on
Name=Value
\emph default
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here is an example batch file 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Input_Pedigree_File=pedin.06
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Input_Locus_File=datain.06
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Input_Map_File=map.06
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Input_Untyped_Ped_Option=2
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Input_Do_Error_Sim=0
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Analysis_Option=Solar
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Chromosome_Single=6
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Traits_Combine=8 9 10 11 12
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Value_Missing_Quant=-9.000000
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Output_Path=mega2_results
\end_layout

