\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
VCF_Marker_Alternative_INFO_Key
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:VCF_Marker_Alternative_INFO_Key"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The marker can be specified as the string associated with the 'ID' field
 of the VCF file, or as the value associated with a key in the 'INFO' field.
 If the user specifies a key (not null) then only the INFO field will be
 used, otherwise only the 'ID' field will be used.
 One or the other is used, never switching between them.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If from this the string value is a '.' (unknown) then the marker will be
 constructed from a prefix ('chr') appending it to the CHROM and POS VCF
 file field values in the following way (chrCHROM_POS).
 This is not guaranteed to be unique since the VCF file specification allows
 multiple records to have the same POS.
 In the construction of this marker name 'X', 'Y', 'XY', and 'MT' will be
 used rather than the associated numbers for the chromosomes.
 This is done in accordance to the species option (See 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Species-options"

\end_inset

) that Mega2 is told to use.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Input_Untyped_Ped_Option
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Input_Untyped_Ped_Option"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This item specifies the handling of marker-untyped pedigrees.
 This is also a necessary item.
 The value should be an integer greater than or equal to 1.
 Values 1-3 select one of the first 3 options of the Untyped pedigree option
 menu .
 Values 4 and onwards refer to the minimum number of the typed persons in
 a pedigree in order for it to be included in the analysis.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 4 corresponds to at least 1 typed person 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 5 corresponds to at least 2 typed persons 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 and so on, i.e.
 included pedigrees must have at least 
\emph on
 
\begin_inset Formula $<$
\end_inset

value
\begin_inset Formula $>$
\end_inset

 - 3 
\emph default
 typed persons.
 
\end_layout

