\begin_layout Paragraph
Trait_Single
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Trait_Single"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option corresponds to the menu option 1 of the Trait reordering menu.
 It should be a positive integer, referring to the list of trait loci present
 in the input data.
 Trait loci are numbered 1 - N (the total number of trait loci) in order
 of their appearance in the locus data file.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 For example, if the locus data file lists loci 10-12 as 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

trait1
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 through 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

trait3
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, specifying a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

1
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 in this option selects 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

trait1
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and so on.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Traits_Loop_Over
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Traits_Loop_Over"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option corresponds to the menu item 2 of the trait reordering menu
 where traits are selected to be analyzed one at a time.
 Trait numbers should correspond to the order in which they are listed in
 the locus file, starting from 1 (as in option 14).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Traits_Combine
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Traits_Combine"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option corresponds to the menu item 3 of the trait reordering menu
 where trait loci are selected to be combined in the same output.
 The actual trait numbers should correspond to the order in which traits
 appear in the locus file, and these numbers can be permuted for the purpose
 of reordering them in the output.
 There should also be an item numbered 
\emph on
N + 1
\emph default
 where N is the number of traits.
 This item refers to the [MARKERS] item displayed in the trait selection
 menu-option 3.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 For options 13, 15 and 16, option 13 takes precedence over the other items,
 and option 15 takes precedence over option 16 i.e.
 if both 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Trait_Single
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Traits_Loop_Over
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 are defined then the latter is ignored.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Trait_Subdirs
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Trait_Subdirs"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These are trait-specific directories in which output files are created if
 the Traits_Loop_Over option is defined.
 The value is a list of strings separated by white-space in a single line.
 The number of directory names read in depend on option 14.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Value_Marker_Compression
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Value_Marker_Compression"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This is an integer value: 1, 2, or 3.
 The default value is 1.
 In this case, each pair of alleles is represented internally with two bits,
 the same as the PLINK compressed binary 'bed' representation.
 This technique does not provide enough space to represent microsatellite
 markers or half-typed genotypes.
 For these data sets, the compression value of 2 should be adequate.
 It provides for up to 256 alleles.
 The compression value of 3 is left for historical comparisons - it should
 never be necessary.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Value_Missing_Quant_On_Input (Value_Missing_Quant is deprecated) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If the list of trait loci selected include one or more quantitative traits
 or covariates, then this value is interpreted as the missing value code
 in the input data.
 The value should be a real number or the string 'NA'.
 In previous versions of Mega2 this item was Value_Missing_Quant, which
 still can be used but is not guaranteed to be supported in future versions
 of Mega2.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Value_Missing_Quant_On_Output
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Value_Missing_Quant_On_Output"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If the list of trait loci that will be output include one or more quantitative
 traits or covariates, then this value is used as the missing quantitative
 phenotype value in the output data for those analysis modes where missing
 values are not predefined (e.g., Merlin uses 'x').
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Value_Affecteds
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "par:Value_Affecteds"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If any of the affection loci selected have more than one liability class,
 then this value refers to the list of 
\begin_inset Formula $<$
\end_inset

status
\begin_inset Formula $>$
\end_inset

-
\begin_inset Formula $<$
\end_inset

class
\begin_inset Formula $>$
\end_inset

 pairs which should be considered affected.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 The value should contain one entry per multiple-liability trait, with white-spa
ce separating each entry.
 Each entry specifies the trait name followed by the list of affection labels,
 and looks like the following: 
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
begin{verbatim}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
ValueAffecteds=TRAIT:2-1,2-3 trt2:2-*
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
end{verbatim}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

*
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 denotes a wild-card e.g., 2-* means status 2 and all classes.
 Similarly 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

*-1
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 would mean all known phenotypes in liability class 1 should be treated
 as being affected.
 Please also consult the affection label definition menu.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Error_Loci 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These and the following options are used by the genotyping error simulation
 module of Mega2.
 This option defines a set of locus numbers at which random genotyping errors
 will be introduced.
 These should be a subset of the marker loci chosen in the locus reordering
 step.
 The number of loci read in depends on option 23.
 The locus numbers are selected from all the loci selected in the reordering
 step.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Error_Except_Loci 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If this option is defined instead of option 21, this list of loci is excepted
 from errors.
 The number of loci read in also depends on option 23 and locus numbers
 refer to the full list of loci selected in the locus-reordering step.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Error_Loci_Num 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The value of this option is a single integer denoting how many markers to
 read in from options 21 or 22.
 It should be a positive integer.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Error_Model 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option specifies the error model to use in error simulation.
 This should be a single character, 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

u
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

U
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 , 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

m
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

M
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 , 
\emph on

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

s
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

S
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\emph default
 .
 They refer to the Uniform error probability model, Marker-specific uniform
 error probability model, and the SimWalk2 error model respectively.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Error_Probabilities 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This option specifies the prior genotyping error probability or probabilities
 for error simulation.
 It should be a single real value, if the model specified in option 24 is
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Uniform
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, or a list of 5 real values, if the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

SimWalk2
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

