\begin_layout Subsection
Non-DOS related problems 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Macintosh users - Note that on your system file-names may be insensitive
 to letter case.
 So, if you create a file map.dat, this is equivalent to having a file MAP.DAT
 (or any combination of uppercase and lower case letters therein).
 Thus, if you try to modify a file named 
\series bold
MAP.DAT
\series default
, you will notice that you are changing 
\series bold
map.dat
\series default
 instead.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 This may cause problems if you use a Mega2 input map file map.dat, then
 create files for SimWalk2 inside the same folder, and run the SimWalk2
 shell script.
 The SimWalk2 map file name is hard-coded as MAP.DAT, therefore the shell
 script creates a copy of the Mega2-created SimWalk2 map file with this
 name prior to each SimWalk2 run.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 Mega2 warns the user if they have used an input map file with the name
 
\series bold
map.dat
\series default
, and selected the SimWalk2 option.
\end_layout

