\begin_layout Standard
Suppose the chromosome number is 5.
 Then Mega2 will, by default, generate the following files (the [*] represents
 different names for each sub-option).
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
   Locus file:           sw2_locus.05   
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
   Pedigree file:        sw2_pedigree.05
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
   Map file:             sw2_map.05     
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
   Penetrance file:      sw2_pen.05     
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
   Simwalk2 batch file:  sw2_batch.05   
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
   C-Shell script:       sw2_haplo.05.sh
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It multiple traits and/or multiple chromosomes are selected for analysis,
 the a combined shell script is created which executes the chromosome-specific
 shell scripts in the individual trait directories.
 This shell script is called 
\series bold
 [*].all.sh 
\series default
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If user selected to set up R-graphics for the non-parametric analysis option,
 then this script will also execute the Rsimwalk2.*.sh script that sets up
 commands for creating postscript files of LOD score plots.
 This ensures that all requires analyses are run before the graphics are
 generated.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Given below is an example of this combined shell script for two traits on
 a single chromosome: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
#----------------------------------------------
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
#   Mega2 version 4.2
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
#   Run date:                2009-4-15-09-49
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
#   This script created on   Wed Apr 15 09:49:08 2009
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
#   Input file names:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
#       Pedigree file:              pedin.01
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
