\begin_layout Standard
Note that the penetrance file will only be created if there are one or more
 affection status loci in the set of selected loci.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset VSpace defskip
\end_inset

 Detailed explanation of the penetrance file:
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 Our penetrance file is designed to permit the user to duplicate precisely
 any analysis done using the LINKAGE package (
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

http://linkage.rockefeller.edu/soft/linkage/
\end_layout

\end_inset

) which relies on liability class coding of the penetrance vectors at the
 disease locus.
 In this approach, the disease locus is assumed to have two alleles, and
 then a person’s penetrance is defined in terms of a vector whose entries
 are the penetrances for the 1/1, 1/2, and 2/2 disease genotypes, in that
 order.
 For example, an autosomal recessive trait with full penetrance would have
 the penetrance vector [0, 0, 1] for the affecteds and the vector [1, 1,
 0] for the normals (if the disease allele is the second allele).
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 To use the penetrance file, you need a set of three matched input files:
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 1) locus.dat 
\begin_inset Formula $<$
\end_inset

- The usual MENDEL locus file.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 2) pedm.dat 
\begin_inset Formula $<$
\end_inset

- The usual MENDEL pedigree file with one quantitative variable representing
 the phenotype at the trait locus.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 3) pen.dat 
\begin_inset Formula $<$
\end_inset

- A penetrance table (created by Mega2).
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 NOTE: The alleles must be listed in the ‘natural’ order in the ‘locus.dat’
 file, so allele ‘1’ is listed first, and allele ‘2’ is listed second.
 Mega2 will do this automatically.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 For each person in the pedigree file, SIMWALK2 (or the USERM15 MENDEL module)
 looks up the appropriate penetrance vector based on the person’s value
 at the quantitative variable (which must be in one-to-one correspondence
 with the disease phenotypes).
 Mega2 does this in the following manner: It takes the affection status
 code (‘1’ = normal, ‘2’ = affected) and multiplies it by 100 and adds to
 the liability class.
 So someone who was coded in the original linkage file as ‘2 4’ (i.e., affected
 in class 4) is assigned the quantitative variable ‘204’ and so we can look
 up the correct penetrance for them in the ‘pen.dat’ file (see example below).
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 Example: 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 If we input this LINKAGE-style datafile into Mega2, then it will generate
 the ‘pen.dat’ file seen below: 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

