\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Reminder: This supports the old FORTRAN-like SAGE format (rather than the
 new more elegant format now available in beta-version which is supported
 by option 22).
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 Provided you have selected only one trait locus (affection status or quantitati
ve), the C-shell script file 'sage.05.sh' will carry out Haseman-Elston linkage
 analyses of the trait versus each of the markers using the SAGE programs
 fsp and sibpal.
 This uses the files sage_ped.05, sage_par.05, sage_loc.05, and sage_sibpal.05.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 The second C-shell script file 'sage_cnt.05.sh' is designed to provide a
 count of all genotyped relative pairs (where an individual is considered
 genotyped if they are genotyped at one or more markers in the input file).
 The ‘sage_cnt.05’ file is a SAGE pedigree file which will contain, for each
 affected, a ‘trait’ which is the total number of genotypes in the input
 file (
\emph on
before
\emph default
 any locus re-ordering) for each affected individual.
