\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Attempting to convert to Mendel output (Option 29) resulted in
 a segmentation fault.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The install.sh installation script incorrectly failed to install
 a binary version when available; it always compiled from source.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The mega2log2html.pl Perl program in some cases tried to read from
 a closed file handle.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Changes from Version 4.0 R5.2 Beta -
\begin_inset Formula $>$
\end_inset

 Version 4.5.3 (Released June 15th, 2011) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Mega2 now supports conversion to IQLS/Idcoefs format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Changes were made towards making Mega2 64-bit compatible.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: The memory allocation routines were enhanced to better report
 out-of-memory errors.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Removed the Python code from the Mega2 source code, replacing
 it with C++ code instead.
 This should avoid installation problems that some users were encountering
 in the Cygwin environment because their Python libraries/headers were out
 of sync with the ones used to compile Mega2.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The use of unique Ped_Per IDs like 1_21 was improperly turned on
 in PAP, so the resulting trip.dat was no longer in proper PAP format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When doing quantitative summaries output to a sub-directory, the
 phenotyping table got written into the subdirectory, but the header got
 written into the root directory.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When converting annotated files to Merlin format, the MEGA2.ERR
 file had two strange extraneous lines at the end.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When converting to Merlin while zeroing out half-typed people,
 the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Half-typed genotypes
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 in MEGA2.RESET was incomplete.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When default batch file options are set to 'yes', Mega2 no longer
 stops at the 'SPLINK option selection' menu when in batch mode.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Under certain conditions, an array storing trait loci indicies
 was too short in the locus reordering function ReOrderLociByPositionNumber.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When only markers were selected, the SUP routine read off the end
 of the line and created incorrect files.
 SUP requires at least one trait locus, so this restriction has been implemented.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Conversion to SLINK format did not work correctly if the trait
 locus was not at the beginning of the locus list.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Corrected behavior of the 'Disease locus selection menu' for the
 SLINK option.
 It was giving the wrong prompt and not correctly indicating the currently
 selected option.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Under certain conditions, one of the theta values was being written
 into the wrong position of the 'theta' array when converting to SLINK format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When setting up for a Quantitative Trait Summary in batch mode,
 the loci were reordered twice when they only needed to be reordered once.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The create_nuked_fids() function, when trying to rename the pedigree
 ID, wrote a string into itself, generating a 'source and destination overlap
 in memcpy' error.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Failed to detect when the input batch file contained a trait number
 out of bounds.
 Added this check in.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: In copy_annotated_to_premake(), there was an error in the logic
 which led to reading a value from beyond the end of the persons[] array.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: There was a failure to initialize the missing_quant value correctly
 when none of the trait loci were quantitative and only the covariates were
 quantitative.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When manually-reordering using the GeneHunter option, the code
 contained an error where it tried to access the '-1' element of the global_trai
t_entries[] array.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: check_map_positions() was not printing error messages properly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The 'Locus Reordering Menu' in the Quantitative Summary option
 was not working correctly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When reading an annotated pedigree file that contains unmapped
 markers (chromosome 'U'), the cumulative counts of markers per chromosomes
 in the chromo_loci_counts array was missing an entry for the 'unknown'
 chromosome.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The 'Select by locus number' option of the 'Locus Reordering Menu'
 was not working correctly when Mega2 was run interactively (It worked correctly
 when Mega2 was run in batch mode).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When attempting to break two loops in a pedigree, Mega2 incorrectly
 assigned proband/loop IDs 1 2 2 2, but this should have been (2,2) (3,3)
 or (1,2) (3,3).
 The person assigned proband ID 1 on input ended up being a member of the
 second loop.
 Since the user can avoid such an error by changing their choice of proband
 or by changing their loop breaker selection criteria, a partial solution
 was implemented so that Mega2 exits whenever it is trying to assign a loop
 breaker who is the proband to a loop other than loop number 2.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: When the user chose to put the output files in a new output folder,
 the resulting MEGA2run.html did not work properly because the time-dated
 summary folder was not being copied into the new output folder.
\end_layout

