\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
PLINK bugs and improvements
\series default
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: PLINK long format output files were not named correctly, as per
 PLINK specifications.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: PLINK shell script had problems and failed to run.
 This has been fixed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Affection status inside the fam file was set to 0 for everyone.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: PLINK map files are now created with genetic distances, by
 using the --cm analysis option.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Allows the creation of output files that are separated by chromosom
es or combined into one set of files.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Mendel bugs and improvements
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Modification: Old format Mendel files are no longer supported within the
 new Mendel option (option 29).
 The old Mendel option (option 2) still continues to produce old Mendel
 format files.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Newest version of Mendel does not accept the variable file, which
 lists quantitative variables, instead quantitative loci are now added to
 the definition file (which is named mendel_locus.* by default).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Modification: Since Mendel expects quantitative variables to be listed at
 the end of the definition file, the user-specified locus order may not
 be honored.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Modification: There was some confusion regarding whether Mendel map file
 should include traits, and these were excluded in the last revision.
 However, it seems that trait loci also need to be in the map file, so they
 have been re-introduced into the map file.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Mendel's newest version now supports longer locus names, up-to
 16 characters long.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Annotated file bugs and improvements 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Enhancement: Mega2 does not require all loci from the names file to be inside
 allele-frequency and penetrance files.
 However, if you do enter a locus in one of these files, it has to be defined
 inside the names file, and it needs to be completely specified, i.e., with
 the required number of frequencies and penetrances.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 If some loci are missing from the frequency file, Mega2 will estimate their
 allele frequencies from the data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Modification:Missing value indicators to the conversion script l2a.py no
 longer need to be enclosed within 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

s.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Mega2 crashed if frequency file was not specified.
 This has been fixed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: The l2a.py conversion script now allows the missing quantitative
 missing value to be specified as a number if no quotes are used, or a string,
 by enclosing your values within quotes.
 Affection and quantitative missing values are interpreted as strings.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: NAs are now acceptable as unknown value indicator for affection
 status loci as well.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize

\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Handling X,Y,XY, and unmapped loci
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Mega2 now allows inclusion of marker loci with unknown positions
 for a limited number of options that do not require a map.
 Unmapped loci can be specified using a special label inside the map file,
 and are output in order of their appearance inside the names file.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Mega2 now implements special handling of Y-linked markers.
 You can create output files for most options using Y-linked markers, but
 note that very few analysis programs do linkage analysis on these.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Menu related changes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: The menu option for changing the unknown status and allele designator
 in the first menu was not working.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Mega2 now allows the user to specify affection labels (lists
 of status-class pairs) separately for each affection trait that has multiple
 liability classes.
 Previously, only a single set of labels was allowed over all traits.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Analysis options and sub-options can now be denoted by their
 names inside the batch file instead of numbers.
 For a list of these names, please consult the documentation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Other bug-fixes and modifications
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Modification: Simwalk2 option output files for haplotype, parametric, non-parame
tric, mistyping-estimation, and IBD estimation are now named sw2_pedigree,
 sw2_locus, sw2_map etc.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Conversion from pre-makeped format to post-makeped format output
 options (such as SLINK, Vitesse etc.) created wrong first-sibling links
 to be created for pedigrees that had half-siblings.
 This has been fixed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bug-fix: Allegro, Gene Hunter, Gene Hunter-Plus and MLB-QTL output locus
 files had default trait penetrances set to 0.0 rather than the usual 0.5.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enhancement: Mega2 automatically limits the display of warnings and error
 messages during the error-checking steps, as these can run into large numbers.
\end_layout

