\begin_layout Subsection*
Bugs in Mega2 4.0 R5.2 Beta 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The use of unique Ped_Per IDs like 1_21 was improperly turned on in PAP,
 so the resulting trip.dat was no longer in proper PAP format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When doing quantitative summaries output to a sub-directory, the phenotyping
 table got written into the subdirectory, but the header got written into
 the root directory.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When converting annotated files to Merlin format, the MEGA2.ERR file had
 two strange extraneous lines at the end.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When converting to Merlin while zeroing out half-typed people, the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Half-typed genotypes
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 in MEGA2.RESET was incomplete.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When default batch file options are set to 'yes', Mega2 no longer stops
 at the 'SPLINK option selection' menu when in batch mode.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Under certain conditions, an array storing trait loci indicies was too short
 in the locus reordering function ReOrderLociByPositionNumber.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When only markers were selected, the SUP routine read off the end of the
 line and created incorrect files.
 SUP requires at least one trait locus, so this restriction has been implemented.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Conversion to SLINK format did not work correctly if the trait locus was
 not at the beginning of the locus list.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Corrected behavior of the 'Disease locus selection menu' for the SLINK option.
 It was giving the wrong prompt and not correctly indicating the currently
 selected option.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Under certain conditions, one of the theta values was being written into
 the wrong position of the 'theta' array when converting to SLINK format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When setting up for a Quantitative Trait Summary in batch mode, the loci
 were reordered twice when they only needed to be reordered once.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The create_nuked_fids() function, when trying to rename the pedigree ID,
 wrote a string into itself, generating a 'source and destination overlap
 in memcpy' error.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Failed to detect when the input batch file contained a trait number out
 of bounds.
 Added this check in.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In copy_annotated_to_premake(), there was an error in the logic which led
 to reading a value from beyond the end of the persons[] array.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There was a failure to initialize the missing_quant value correctly when
 none of the trait loci were quantitative and only the covariates were quantitat
ive.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When manually-reordering using the GeneHunter option, the code contained
 an error where it tried to access the '-1' element of the global_trait_entries[
] array.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The check_map_positions() function was not printing error messages properly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 'Locus Reordering Menu' in the Quantitative Summary option was not working
 correctly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When reading an annotated pedigree file that contains unmapped markers (chromoso
me 'U'), the cumulative counts of markers per chromosomes in the chromo_loci_cou
nts array was missing an entry for the 'unknown' chromosome.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 'Select by locus number' option of the 'Locus Reordering Menu' was not
 working correctly when Mega2 was run interactively (It worked correctly
 when Mega2 was run in batch mode).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When attempting to break two loops in a pedigree, Mega2 incorrectly assigned
 proband/loop IDs 1 2 2 2, but this should have been (2,2) (3,3) or (1,2)
 (3,3).
 The person assigned proband ID 1 on input ended up being a member of the
 second loop.
 Since the user can avoid such an error by changing their choice of proband
 or by changing their loop breaker selection criteria, a partial solution
 was implemented so that Mega2 exits whenever it is trying to assign a loopbreak
er who is the proband to a loop other than loop number 2.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When the user chose to put the output files in a new output folder, the
 resulting MEGA2run.html did not work properly because the time-dated summary
 folder was not being copied into the new output folder.
\end_layout

